WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.270
Dear Paul,
亲爱的保罗：

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.020
I’m glad to offer some advice on your oral report.
我很高兴为你的口头报告提一些建议。

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:16.840
First, choose a scientist whose story interests you, such as Zhang Heng, who invented the world’s first instrument for detecting earthquakes.
首先，选择一位故事能引起你兴趣的科学家，比如张衡，他发明了世界上第一台检测地震的仪器。

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:26.040
Next, collect reliable information from library books and museum websites, focusing on the scientist’s major achievements and their influence.
其次，从图书馆的书籍和博物馆网站上收集可靠的资料，重点关注这位科学家的主要成就及其影响。

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:35.580
Then, organize your report around one or two vivid stories rather than a long list of facts, and use pictures or models to make it more engaging.
然后，围绕一两个生动的故事来组织报告，而不是罗列一长串事实，并借助图片或模型让报告更吸引人。

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:40.850
Finally, rehearse several times so that you can speak fluently and confidently.
最后，排练几遍，这样你就能讲得流利而自信。

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.040
I hope these tips help.
希望这些建议对你有帮助。

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.290
Good luck with your report!
祝你报告顺利！

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.120
Yours, Li Ming
你的朋友，李明
